                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_334">London, London,
                        Charterhouse of the Salutation of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p><q>Liber S.
                           Matildae inscr. Liber spiritualis Gratiae. Speculum Sacerdotum sec.
                           visionem et exhortationem S. Edwardi Regis et Confessoris. Uterque liber
                           transcriptus est a <persName role="scr">Joh. Whetham</persName> Monacho
                           Carth. Londinensi anno 1513. Adjic. Itinerarium Johannis de Hese
                           Presbyteri Trajectensis Dioc. ab Hierusolyma anno 1489 per diversas mundi
                           partes. in 4.</q> Description taken from <title>Librorum manuscriptorum
                           in bibliotheca <persName role="fmo">Jacobi Waraei</persName> equitis Aur.
                           Catalogus</title> (Dublin 1648), Theol. MS. 12</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName type="fmo">Sir James
                        Ware</persName> in 1648. Compare citation above.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Henry, Earl of
                        Clarendon</persName> in 1697. CMA 2.2.110 (where the scribe's name is given
                     as Joh. Wallam). This was the last known location reported in the second
                     edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). The book remains
                     untraced.</provenance>
